// F11 — a module another module can import. Ticket 40 §1: the module's atom is
// its FULL dotted path, so this emits 'Shop.Collections.Ints' and `ls` shows a
// file of that name. Nothing about the tag mint (26 §1) moves — it was always
// written against the module atom rather than against a single segment.
//
//   bsc examples/Shop/Reports/Totals.bs Restate 3
//
module Shop.Collections.Ints

public int Sum(list<int> xs, int acc)
Sum([], acc)          -> acc
Sum([x, ..rest], acc) -> Sum(rest, acc + x)

private int Length(list<int> xs, int acc)
Length([], acc)          -> acc
Length([x, ..rest], acc) -> Length(rest, acc + 1)

// Ticket 40 §2: arity overloading is PERMITTED — the BEAM's own identity rule,
// unmodified. `Length/2` above and `Length/1` here are two functions, and before
// F11 the checker could not represent that: callees were keyed by name alone, so
// `maps:from_list/1` kept whichever was written last.
public int Length(list<int> xs)
Length(xs) -> Length(xs, 0)
